// ── Notification Templates (P0 forward-reference resolved) ────────────────────
// S5 DECISION: Custom BullMQ-based notification service (not Novu).
// Rationale documented in docs/CHANGELOG.md S5:
//   - Novu adds a cloud dependency (data sovereignty concern under NDPR 2019)
//   - Institution data cannot leave Nigeria in many state university policies
//   - Custom service using BullMQ + SMTP (Postal/Mailgun NG) + Termii SMS API
//     handles all cases and keeps PII within the institution's infrastructure
//   - If a future institution explicitly accepts Novu's DPA, the notification
//     worker can be swapped out — the outbox → BullMQ job interface is unchanged
// NOTE: a `NotificationChannel` model previously lived here (per-institution
// provider config: SMTP/Termii/Firebase credentials). It had no migration —
// "notification_channels" was never created in Postgres — and no service
// code referenced it (confirmed by repo-wide search); it also collided by
// name with the NotificationChannelType enum above. Removed as dead,
// non-functional schema rather than retrofitted, since nothing depends on
// it. If per-institution provider config becomes a real requirement, model
// it under a non-colliding name (e.g. `NotificationProviderConfig`) with a
// matching migration from the start. Audit remediation — see
// docs/CHANGELOG.md, item R1.

